$Enabled = $false;
      $Triggers = @();
      $Task = Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName "ShadowCopyVolume$($VolumeID)" -ea SilentlyContinue
      if ($Task -ne $null)
      {
        $TaskInfo = $Task | Get-ScheduledTaskInfo
        $Enabled = $Task.State -ne "Disabled";
        foreach ($Trigger in $Task.Triggers)
        {
            $object = New-Object -typeName PSObject
            $object | Add-Member -Type NoteProperty -Name "Start" -Value ([DateTime]::Parse($Trigger.StartBoundary)) [...] > Configure Shadow Copies) you can Disabled or Enabled each volume for shadow copy. You can see in attach images "Volume" and "Next Run time" ("Time" or "Disabled" status).

I looking for stript in powerhsell that list information which I can see in GUI?

I have tried `vssadmin list volumes` or `Get-CimInstance Win32_ShadowCopy` but I need detect if VSS on specific Volume is Enabled or Disabled.

Please, does anybody know this issue?

Thank you for you answers and your help! [...] $VSSDriveLetter = $($configuration[$count + 2]).Trim()
